The proof follows via $\ensuremath{\varepsilon}$-net.  Let $\bm{A}$ be any rank at most $2r$ matrix such that $\|\bm{A}\|_F\leq 1$.  Then $\langle \bm{H}, \bm{A} \rangle$ is Gaussian with variance at most $2 \|\bm{A}\|_F^2 \leq 2$.  Hoeffding's inequality implies that $\bigg| \langle \bm{H},\bm{A} \rangle \bigg| \leq C t$ with probability at least $1 - 2 \exp( - c t^2)$.  Next, let $\mathcal{N}_{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}$ be a covering of rank at most $2r$ matrices of Frobenius norm at most 1; by Lemma 3.1 of \citet{candes_tight_2011}, it holds that $|\mathcal{N}_{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}| \leq \bigg( \frac{9}{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}} \bigg)^{3 dr}$.  The union bound implies that
\begin{align}
    \sup_{\bm{A} \in \mathcal{N}_{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}} \bigg| \langle \bm{H},\bm{A} \rangle \bigg| \leq C t
\end{align}
with probability at least $1 - 2\exp( 3dr \log (9/\ensuremath{\varepsilon}) - t^2 )$.  Taking $t \geq \sqrt{dr}$ shows that this probability is at most $1 - 2 \exp( - c d r)$ as desired.

For the other event it holds that $\frac{\|\bm{g}\|}{\sqrt{n}}$ is a $\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}$-Lipschitz function of $\bm{g}$ and consequently the event holds with probability at least $1 - 2\exp( - c n)$.  The bound on $\|\bm{H}\|$ follows directly from \citet{bandeira_sharp_2016}.

First, fix any $\bm{U} \in \mathbb{B}(\bm{\widehat U},K)$.    Define the function
\begin{align}
